// Canonical walk-in economy = PROJECT_DEFINITION §7.5 (task 07b; keys are wire/save-stable).
// Buyer semantics (2026-07-17, task 19 / ADR-13): the vessel is the BUYER of berth time.
//   target_price_range        = the hidden BUDGET CEILING (top the vessel will pay; a player
//                               fee demand is accepted only at or below it).
//   min_acceptable_price_range = the OPENING-ASK basis (vessel opens low at ~0.70-0.85 x target;
//                               the player negotiates the fee UPWARD toward the ceiling).
// The original task-15 engine read these seller-inverted; RealNegotiationEngine was rewritten.
// Values are unchanged — only the reading is corrected.
// Live-time patience recalibration (2026-07-17, task 24 / ADR-14):
//   max_wait_minutes_range     = the hidden patience window in SIM-minutes, enforced by
//                               TimeoutWithdrawalBehaviour against elapsed sim time. Until task
//                               24 the clock never advanced, so the stub-era 5-40 sim-min values
//                               were never exercised; at the default 300 s/game-day mapping
//                               (1 sim-min ≈ 0.208 wall-s) they would time every walk-in out
//                               1-8 WALL-seconds after hailing. Rescaled ~x14-x20 so windows land
//                               around Settings.timeLimitSeconds (60 real-s nominal): ferry
//                               (scheduled, impatient) < container (brisk) < tanker = cruise <
//                               cargo (pragmatic, most patient) — the task-07 relative ordering,
//                               preserved. §7.5 price columns untouched.
// Task 19b (§7.3 duration bargaining):
//   min_duration_range         = the draw range of the HIDDEN cargo-handling floor (hours). The
//                               spawn clamps the draw to the vessel's announced preferred stay
//                               (6..18h), so floor <= preferred always. The floor's FIELD never
//                               goes on the wire (P-04); its value surfaces only as the hours
//                               term of a "we need at least Nh" counter.
